{Occupation: ("Prince of the Armada" + "Leader of the Invasion of Earth" + "Frustrated, Overlooked Heir to Mavro's Throne")}  

{Background: ("Prince Vekar is the eldest son of Emperor Mavro and the older brother of Vrak. Unlike his cunning and ruthless brother, Vekar is impulsive, arrogant, and frequently makes mistakes due to his overconfidence. Despite leading numerous invasions across the galaxy, his father never truly respected him, seeing him as foolish and incompetent. This fueled Vekar’s deep-seated insecurities and desperation to prove himself as a capable ruler.  

Despite being given command of the Armada’s Earth invasion, his father placed Damaras as his second-in-command, a move Vekar saw as both insulting and unnecessary. He constantly sought to outshine his brother’s accomplishments, but his hot temper and unwillingness to take advice led to repeated failures. These failures caused him to lash out at his subordinates, though deep down, he cared about Argus and Levira, showing genuine distress over Argus's death.  

Vekar's desperate desire for validation peaked when his father gifted him the **Armada Megazord**, believing that his victory over the Rangers would finally earn him the respect he craved. However, his overconfidence proved to be his undoing. After Argus was slain, he recklessly piloted his Megazord into battle, only to be consumed in its explosion, leading to his ultimate demise. Even in death, Vekar remained a tragic figure—a prince who longed to be seen as more than a fool but never overcame his own flaws.")}  

{Powers: ("No Natural Combat Abilities" + "Relies Entirely on His Fleet and Subordinates")}  

{Abilities: ("Incredible Leaper" + "Expert Pilot of the Armada Megazord")}  

{Arsenal: ("Armada Megazord: A powerful war machine gifted by his father, second only to the Armada Mothership in strength. It bore a resemblance to Vekar himself, symbolizing his royal status.")}
